// title: Mission Passed (boss)
// xp: 100
// boss: true
// hidden: wanted #test("heist, heist")[5]
// hidden: wanted #test("speeding, pay-n-spray, carjack")[2]
// hidden: wanted #test("bribe, speeding")[1]
// hidden: banner #test("speeding")["★☆☆☆☆"]
// hidden: banner #test("heist, carjack, speeding")["WASTED"]
// hint: Split the log into events and walk them, keeping the level in a `var`; a `match` on the event's text tells how it changes the level.
// hint: Clamp the level after every event, not once at the end: a pay-n-spray after six stars must still end at zero, and a bribe can't go below it. For the banner, strings have `repeat`.
//
// Los Santos keeps score. The police log for a night out is a list of
// events separated by `", "`, and each moves your wanted level:
//
// - `speeding` adds one star, `carjack` two, `heist` three;
// - `bribe` takes one away;
// - `pay-n-spray` clears them all (a fresh coat of paint; the cops never
//   recognise you);
// - anything else, like `jaywalking`, the LSPD doesn't care about.
//
// The level never goes below zero or above five stars, after every event.
// Write:
//
// - `wanted(log)`: the level at the end of the night;
// - `banner(log)`: the level as five stars, filled `★` then empty `☆`
//   (`"★★☆☆☆"` for two), except at five, which is `"WASTED"`.
//
// *Mission passed! Respect +.*
#test("speeding, carjack")[3]
#test("heist, heist, pay-n-spray, speeding")[1]
#test("bribe, bribe")[0]
#test("jaywalking")[0]
fun wanted(log: str) -> int {
    // TODO
    return 0
}

#test("speeding, carjack")["★★★☆☆"]
#test("jaywalking")["☆☆☆☆☆"]
#test("heist, heist")["WASTED"]
fun banner(log: str) -> str {
    // TODO
    return ""
}
